                  <provenance cert="low"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_595">Winchester, Hampshire. College
                        of St Mary the Virgin of Winchester</orgName><p>Flyleaves of this bursars'
                        account book for the years 1556--8 are four folios from a late 14th-cent.
                        English copy of William de Mandagout's De electionibus. There may be a
                        presumption that the scrap for these flyleaves was sourced locally, and
                        indeed may well belong to the copy given to the library by the fellow Robert
                        Keton (d. 1429) and reported in the inventory in the Liber Albus, fol.
                        35v.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Robert Keton (d. 1429), fellow of Winchester,
                     by whom given to the college.</provenance>
